# Binary assets — never normalise line endings or diff.
# Text files keep the repository's existing checkout behaviour (core.autocrlf);
# the web test helpers normalise CRLF->LF at their read point, so they pass on
# both a CRLF (windows CI) and an LF checkout. Do not add a global text/eol rule:
# the committed blobs of the help/guide content are LF (core.eol=lf), and its tests
# assert that against the git object, not against the checkout, so the assertions
# hold on any shape; a text/eol rule now would store nothing different and would
# make a repository-wide renormalisation the next required step.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.wasm binary
*.pdf binary
*.bin binary
*.dat binary